===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To send to the masthead as a [[punishment]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1838|author=w:Frederick Marryat|title=Rattlin the Reefer|passage=“I was '''mast-headed''', sir.” <br>“'''Mast-headed'''! how - for what?”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Gregory Fremont-Barnes|title=Nelson's Officers and Midshipmen|page=30
|passage=When the ship happened to be in a warm climate, '''mastheading''' constituted a fairly mild punishment; indeed, many regarded it as rather a relief from duty. But in inclement weather the experience was most unpleasant.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To furnish (a newspaper) with a masthead.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1991|author=John Costello|title=Ten Days to Destiny|page=542
|passage=It was '''mastheaded''' as "Palatka's Only Independent Home-Owned Newspaper."}}

